> Also, how can I acquire more waters, either holy or otherwise?
 
Aside from finding them in shops or laying around?

Cancel or dilute other potions, or dip a unicorn horn in them.

#Dip a unicorn horn into the potion to turn potions of hallucination, 
blindness, and confusion into water. (nb, take appropriate precautions 
until you know that what you're dipping into isn't a potion of 
polymorph.)

To cancel potions, zap them with a wand or spell of cancellation. 
(Though frankly you'll usually have far better uses for limited wand 
charges.) Most potions will become water; some will not change (fruit 
joice, oil, booze) and some (see invisible, sickness) will become fruit 
juice.

To dilute potions, dip them in water, twice. You can:
* Dip in a fountain (with possible major negative effects)
* Dip in a body of water while wearing water walking boots
* Go swimming (drop everything you're carrying or wearing that you 
don't want to get wet, and walk into a body of water. If you're wearing 
an amulet of magical breating, you can then just dip your potions. If 
you're not wearing an amulet of magical breating, as long as you're not 
burdened and there's a square of solid ground next to the water, you'll 
crawl out the next turn, and there's a chance that every item in your 
inventory will be diluted (potions), blanked (scrolls and spellbooks), 
or rusted (rustables). The potions (and scrolls, and rustables AFAIK) 
have a save throw, so it will likely take several iterations to get 
everything diluted to water.

See http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/pot2-343.txt for a complete 
discussion.

